      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Dealing with disruptive personalities often requires a firmer approach. Although you should still work within the bounds of your progressive discipline policy, you may need to accelerate the process due to the egregious nature of the behavior. Document all incidents with specifics, focusing on how the individual's actions affect the team and organization's functioning. If necessary, you might skip some steps, like forgoing a written warning before moving to a suspension. Nonetheless, it's crucial to still follow legal procedures and practices. Keep in mind that having a history of such behavior can shorten these steps, but you should still ensure fairness and impartiality at all stages. Consulting with HR or legal departments could also help navigate these situations more effectively and legally.",
